    "body": "Hi, I believe you're mistaken. qBittorrent works fine with IPv6 UDP trackers, my settings are the same as your screenshot, and newTrackon doesn't use any qBittorrent code, it has its own implementation. Another example to show `udp://tracker2.itzmx.com:6961/announce` is actually not responding to UDP packets is just using `udp://tracker3.itzmx.com:6961/announce`, which is also a IPv6-only tracker, also hosted in Hetzner:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/CorralPeltzer/newTrackon/assets/6959494/2e37d58a-b156-4992-87c4-d1322fb68ae4)\r\n\r\nLooking at the packets in wireshark, you can observe `udp://tracker3.itzmx.com:6961/announce` (IP is `2a01:4f8:c012:8025::6961`):\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/CorralPeltzer/newTrackon/assets/6959494/784bcee3-4c0d-45a0-8985-2e464ea1464d)\r\n\r\nBut no response from `udp://tracker2.itzmx.com:6961/announce` (IP `2a01:4f8:c012:8025::`):\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/CorralPeltzer/newTrackon/assets/6959494/197180a4-e54d-402f-a6a1-14ed32eefdec)\r\n\r\nIn your wireshark screenshot, it seems you're actually getting responses from tracker3.",
